---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Exponential Growth Calculator – Growth & Decay Calculator"
  description="Calculate exponential growth or decay over time. Solve for final quantity, initial quantity, growth/decay rate, or time periods with step-by-step mathematical solutions."
  category="Math"
  calculatorName="Exponential Growth Calculator"
  slug="exponential-growth-calculator"
  keywords={[
    'exponential growth calculator',
    'exponential decay calculator',
    'growth rate calculator',
    'exponential growth formula',
    'exponential decay formula',
    'doubling time calculator',
    'half life calculator',
    'calculate exponential growth',
    'exponential growth equation',
    'continuous growth calculator',
    'population growth calculator'
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">

    <!-- Calculator Card Container (Matches BMI Calculator Layout) -->
    <div
      class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-slate-50 to-emerald-50/60 p-1.5 shadow-xl shadow-slate-900/5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-950 dark:to-emerald-950/20"
    >
      <!-- Top Solve-For Tabs (Styled exactly like BMI Unit Tabs) -->
      <div
        class="flex items-center gap-1 border-b border-slate-300/80 px-2 pt-1 pb-0 dark:border-slate-800 overflow-x-auto scrollbar-thin"
      >
        <button
          type="button"
          id="tab-final"
          data-target="final"
          class="solve-tab active rounded-t-xl border-t border-x border-slate-300/90 bg-white px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs -mb-px dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white transition cursor-pointer shrink-0"
        >
          Final Quantity x(t)
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="tab-initial"
          data-target="initial"
          class="solve-tab rounded-t-xl bg-blue-700/90 px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-white hover:bg-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-800 dark:hover:bg-blue-700 transition cursor-pointer shrink-0"
        >
          Initial Quantity x₀
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="tab-rate"
          data-target="rate"
          class="solve-tab rounded-t-xl bg-blue-700/90 px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-white hover:bg-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-800 dark:hover:bg-blue-700 transition cursor-pointer shrink-0"
        >
          Growth/Decay Rate (r)
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="tab-time"
          data-target="time"
          class="solve-tab rounded-t-xl bg-blue-700/90 px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-white hover:bg-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-800 dark:hover:bg-blue-700 transition cursor-pointer shrink-0"
        >
          Time / Periods (t)
        </button>
      </div>

      <!-- Main Inputs Form Box -->
      <form
        id="growth-form"
        class="space-y-4 bg-white/45 p-4 sm:p-6 dark:bg-slate-950/40"
        novalidate
        onsubmit="return false;"
      >
        <!-- Mode Subtitle & Period Unit Switcher (Matches BMI Classification Switcher) -->
        <div
          class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800/80 text-xs"
        >
          <span id="solve-mode-subtitle" class="font-bold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Target: Solve for Final Quantity x(t)
          </span>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <label for="select-time-unit" class="font-semibold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Time Unit:</label>
            <select
              id="select-time-unit"
              class="rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-800 focus:border-blue-500 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer"
            >
              <option value="years">Years</option>
              <option value="months">Months</option>
              <option value="days">Days</option>
              <option value="hours">Hours</option>
              <option value="periods" selected>Periods</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 1: Initial Quantity (x₀) -->
        <div
          id="row-x0"
          class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[140px_1fr] items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4"
        >
          <label
            for="input-x0"
            class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
          >
            Initial Quantity (x₀)
          </label>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
            <div class="relative flex items-center w-40 sm:w-52">
              <input
                type="number"
                id="input-x0"
                value=""
                step="any"
                placeholder="Enter initial value"
                class="w-full rounded-lg border-2 border-slate-400/80 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white"
                autocomplete="off"
              />
            </div>
            <span
              id="badge-x0-target"
              class="text-xs font-medium text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400"
            >
              baseline quantity at t = 0
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 2: Growth / Decay Rate (r %) -->
        <div
          id="row-rate"
          class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[140px_1fr] items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4"
        >
          <label
            for="input-rate"
            class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
          >
            Rate (r %)
          </label>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
            <div class="relative flex items-center w-40 sm:w-52">
              <input
                type="number"
                id="input-rate"
                value=""
                step="any"
                placeholder="e.g. 5 or -10"
                class="w-full rounded-lg border-2 border-slate-400/80 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white pr-9"
                autocomplete="off"
              />
              <span
                class="pointer-events-none absolute right-3 text-xs font-bold text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400"
              >
                %
              </span>
            </div>
            <span
              id="badge-rate-target"
              class="text-xs font-medium text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400"
            >
              positive (+) for growth, negative (−) for decay
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 3: Time / Periods (t) -->
        <div
          id="row-time"
          class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[140px_1fr] items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4"
        >
          <label
            for="input-time"
            class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
          >
            Time Periods (t)
          </label>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
            <div class="relative flex items-center w-40 sm:w-52">
              <input
                type="number"
                id="input-time"
                value=""
                step="any"
                placeholder="Enter periods"
                class="w-full rounded-lg border-2 border-slate-400/80 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white pr-16"
                autocomplete="off"
              />
              <span
                id="unit-label-input"
                class="pointer-events-none absolute right-3 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-medium"
              >
                periods
              </span>
            </div>
            <span
              id="badge-time-target"
              class="text-xs font-medium text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400"
            >
              elapsed duration
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 4: Final Quantity (x(t)) -->
        <div
          id="row-xt"
          class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[140px_1fr] items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4"
        >
          <label
            for="input-xt"
            class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
          >
            Final Quantity x(t)
          </label>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
            <div class="relative flex items-center w-40 sm:w-52">
              <input
                type="number"
                id="input-xt"
                value=""
                step="any"
                placeholder="To be calculated"
                disabled
                class="w-full rounded-lg border-2 border-dashed border-slate-300 bg-slate-100/70 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-500 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900/60 dark:text-slate-500 cursor-not-allowed"
                autocomplete="off"
              />
            </div>
            <span
              id="badge-xt-target"
              class="rounded-full bg-blue-100 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold text-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-950 dark:text-blue-300"
            >
              Target to Solve
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 5: Action Buttons (BMI Exact Match: Green Calculate ▶ and Gray Clear) -->
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 pt-3">
          <button
            type="submit"
            id="btn-calculate"
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-emerald-600 px-6 py-2.5 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-emerald-600/20 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-emerald-700 active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer"
          >
            <span>Calculate</span>
            <span
              class="flex h-5 w-5 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-white/20 text-[10px]"
            >
              ▶
            </span>
          </button>
          <button
            type="button"
            id="btn-clear"
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-slate-400 hover:bg-slate-500 dark:bg-slate-600 dark:hover:bg-slate-500 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-white shadow-sm active:scale-[0.98] transition cursor-pointer"
          >
            Clear
          </button>
        </div>

        <!-- Error Banner -->
        <p
          id="growth-error"
          class="hidden rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 px-3 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 dark:border-red-900/60 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-300"
          role="alert"
          aria-live="polite"
        >
        </p>
      </form>
    </div>

    <!-- Initial Prompt Placeholder (Shown before Calculate is clicked, exactly like BMI Calculator) -->
    <div
      id="results-placeholder"
      class="rounded-2xl border border-dashed border-slate-300 bg-slate-50/60 p-8 text-center dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/40"
    >
      <div
        class="mx-auto flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-100 text-xl text-emerald-700 dark:bg-emerald-950 dark:text-emerald-300"
      >
        📈
      </div>
      <h3 class="mt-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Ready to Calculate Exponential Growth & Decay
      </h3>
      <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 max-w-md mx-auto">
        Fill in your parameters above and click the green <strong>"Calculate ▶"</strong> button to view the computed values, trajectory curve, and step-by-step breakdown.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Calculation Results Card (Revealed on Submit, matches BMI Calculator Layout) -->
    <div
      id="results-card"
      class="hidden rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/95 p-5 shadow-xs transition dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/90 sm:p-6 space-y-6"
    >
      <!-- Top Section: Main Output & Classification -->
      <div
        class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4 border-b border-slate-200 pb-5 dark:border-slate-800"
      >
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span
              id="res-target-label"
              class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400"
            >
              Calculated Final Quantity x(t)
            </span>
            <span
              id="res-doubling-tag"
              class="rounded-full bg-slate-200 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold text-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300"
            >
              Doubling Time: —
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-3">
            <span
              id="res-primary-val"
              class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-mono"
            >
              —
            </span>
            <span
              id="res-nature-badge"
              class="rounded-full bg-emerald-100 px-3.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-950/80 dark:text-emerald-300"
            >
              Exponential Growth ⚡
            </span>
          </div>
          <p id="res-subtitle" class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-mono">
            Starting from x₀ over t periods
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="flex sm:flex-col items-center sm:items-end justify-between gap-1 text-xs"
        >
          <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
            Growth Factor (M): <span id="res-factor" class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-mono">—</span>
          </div>
          <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
            Continuous Rate (k): <span id="res-k" class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-mono">—</span>
          </div>
          <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
            Total Change: <span id="res-abs-change" class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-mono">—</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Parameter Summary Cards (like BMI prime/ponderal/healthy weight breakdown) -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-3.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 block">Initial Value (x₀)</span>
          <div id="stat-x0" class="text-sm sm:text-base font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-mono mt-0.5">—</div>
          <span class="text-[10px] text-slate-400">Baseline at t = 0</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-3.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 block">Periodic Rate (r)</span>
          <div id="stat-rate" class="text-sm sm:text-base font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-mono mt-0.5">—</div>
          <span class="text-[10px] text-slate-400">Per time unit</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-3.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 block">Total Periods (t)</span>
          <div id="stat-time" class="text-sm sm:text-base font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-mono mt-0.5">—</div>
          <span class="text-[10px] text-slate-400">Duration</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-3.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 block">Overall Change %</span>
          <div id="stat-pct" class="text-sm sm:text-base font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-mono mt-0.5">—</div>
          <span class="text-[10px] text-slate-400">Total percentage</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Trajectory Curve Plot (matches BMI Visual Gauge Card style) -->
      <div
        class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-4 sm:p-6 shadow-xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900"
      >
        <div
          class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-slate-100 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800/80 mb-3"
        >
          <h4
            class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5"
          >
            <span>📈</span> Exponential Trajectory Curve
          </h4>
          <span
            id="curve-range-label"
            class="rounded-full bg-blue-50 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[11px] font-semibold text-blue-700 dark:bg-blue-950/60 dark:text-blue-300 font-mono"
          >
            t = 0 to t
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="relative w-full h-44 sm:h-52 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/50 rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-200/60 dark:border-slate-800">
          <svg id="svg-curve" class="w-full h-full" viewBox="0 0 500 200" preserveAspectRatio="none">
            <line x1="0" y1="50" x2="500" y2="50" stroke="currentColor" class="text-slate-200 dark:text-slate-800" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <line x1="0" y1="100" x2="500" y2="100" stroke="currentColor" class="text-slate-200 dark:text-slate-800" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <line x1="0" y1="150" x2="500" y2="150" stroke="currentColor" class="text-slate-200 dark:text-slate-800" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <path id="svg-path" d="" fill="none" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
            <circle id="svg-dot-start" cx="0" cy="0" r="5" fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width="2" />
            <circle id="svg-dot-end" cx="0" cy="0" r="6" fill="#10b981" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width="2" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-[11px] text-slate-500 mt-2 font-mono">
          <span id="label-plot-start">Initial (t=0)</span>
          <span id="label-plot-end">Final (t)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step-by-Step Derivation & Table (matches BMI classification & healthy weight tables) -->
      <div
        class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-4 sm:p-6 shadow-xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900"
      >
        <div
          class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-slate-100 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800/80 mb-3"
        >
          <h4
            class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5"
          >
            <span>📝</span> Step-by-Step Mathematical Solution
          </h4>
        </div>
        <ol id="res-steps" class="space-y-1.5 text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-decimal list-inside font-mono leading-relaxed"></ol>
      </div>

      <!-- Period Table -->
      <div
        class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-4 sm:p-6 shadow-xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900"
      >
        <div
          class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-slate-100 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800/80 mb-3"
        >
          <div>
            <h4
              class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5"
            >
              <span>📊</span> Period-by-Period Value Table
            </h4>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 mt-0.5">Progression increments (capped at 50 rows)</p>
          </div>
          <span
            id="table-badge-rows"
            class="text-[11px] font-bold text-slate-500 bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg"
          >
            0 rows
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto max-h-64 scrollbar-thin">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden font-mono">
            <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-900 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 sticky top-0">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-2.5">Period (t)</th>
                <th class="p-2.5">Quantity x(t)</th>
                <th class="p-2.5">Change (Δ)</th>
                <th class="p-2.5">% Change</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="table-body" class="divide-y divide-slate-200 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ======================================================== -->
  <!-- EDUCATIONAL CONTENT & COMPREHENSIVE GUIDE                -->
  <!-- ======================================================== -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">What Is Exponential Growth?</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <strong>Exponential growth</strong> describes a process where a quantity multiplies by a constant factor over equal intervals of time, rather than adding a fixed numerical amount. Because the increase in each period is directly proportional to the size of the quantity at that moment, exponential growth accelerates over time: the larger the quantity becomes, the faster it expands.
        </p>
        <p>
          In contrast to <em>linear growth</em> (which adds a constant increment such as +10 per year), exponential change compounds repeatedly. An investment growing at 5% per year, a bacterial colony doubling every 20 minutes, or a population expanding steadily all represent exponential multiplication.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">The Core Exponential Growth Formula</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          For discrete intervals (such as annual compounding, monthly growth, or daily reproduction cycles), the governing mathematical equation is:
        </p>
        <div class="my-3 rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/50 p-4 font-mono text-center text-base sm:text-lg font-black text-blue-700 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:bg-blue-950/40 dark:text-blue-300">
          x(t) = x₀ × (1 + r / 100)ᵗ
        </div>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside">
          <li><strong>x(t):</strong> The final quantity remaining or accumulated after <em>t</em> periods have elapsed.</li>
          <li><strong>x₀:</strong> The initial or starting quantity at the reference point (<em>t = 0</em>).</li>
          <li><strong>r:</strong> The percentage growth or decay rate per unit period (expressed as a percentage, e.g., 5 for 5%).</li>
          <li><strong>t:</strong> The number of elapsed time periods (years, months, days, or custom intervals).</li>
          <li><strong>1 + r/100:</strong> The growth factor or multiplier (<em>M</em>). For example, a 5% growth rate yields <em>M = 1.05</em>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Exponential Growth vs. Exponential Decay</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          The sign and magnitude of the rate parameter <em>r</em> establish whether the system undergoes growth or decay:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-2">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50/50 p-4 dark:border-emerald-900/60 dark:bg-emerald-950/20">
            <h3 class="font-extrabold text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>📈</span> Exponential Growth (r &gt; 0)
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 leading-relaxed">
              When <em>r &gt; 0</em>, the multiplier <em>1 + r/100 &gt; 1</em>. The quantity increases with compounding rapidity over time. Examples include population expansions, compound interest, and viral reproduction.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-rose-200 bg-rose-50/50 p-4 dark:border-rose-900/60 dark:bg-rose-950/20">
            <h3 class="font-extrabold text-rose-800 dark:text-rose-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>📉</span> Exponential Decay (−100% &lt; r &lt; 0)
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-rose-900 dark:text-rose-200 leading-relaxed">
              When <em>r &lt; 0</em>, the multiplier satisfies <em>0 &lt; 1 + r/100 &lt; 1</em>. The quantity decreases toward zero over successive periods. Examples include radioactive half-life decay, depreciation, and drug clearance in pharmacology.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
          <strong>The −100% Limit:</strong> If <em>r = −100%</em>, the multiplier becomes <em>1 + (−100/100) = 0</em>, meaning the quantity is instantly depleted to zero. Rates below −100% would produce a negative base multiplier, which produces non-real complex numbers for fractional time powers and is mathematically invalid for real physical quantities.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">How to Calculate the Time Needed to Reach a Target</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          When you know the initial amount <em>x₀</em>, the final goal <em>x(t)</em>, and the growth rate <em>r</em>, you can solve for the required elapsed time <em>t</em> by applying natural logarithms:
        </p>
        <div class="my-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 font-mono text-center text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-800 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950 dark:text-slate-200">
          t = ln(x(t) / x₀) / ln(1 + r / 100)
        </div>
        <p>
          <strong>Worked Target Example:</strong> Suppose you have an initial investment of 10,000 growing at 5% annually and want to know when it reaches 30,000 (a 3× multiple):
        </p>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-3 text-xs font-mono dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950">
          t = ln(30,000 / 10,000) / ln(1 + 5/100) = ln(3) / ln(1.05) ≈ 1.09861 / 0.04879 ≈ 22.52 periods (years)
        </div>
        <p>
          Thus, it takes approximately 22.5 years for the capital to triple under constant 5% annual growth.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Can Time (t) Be Negative in Exponential Formulas?</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <strong>Yes.</strong> Mathematically, time <em>t</em> is not restricted to positive values. A negative time represents <strong>looking backward into the past</strong> prior to the chosen baseline observation time (<em>t = 0</em>).
        </p>
        <p>
          For example, if a population is 121 today with a constant 10% growth rate, setting <em>t = −2</em> evaluates:
        </p>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-3 text-xs font-mono dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950">
          x(−2) = 121 × (1.10)⁻² = 121 / (1.10)² = 121 / 1.21 = 100
        </div>
        <p>
          This indicates that 2 periods before the reference point, the population was exactly 100.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Continuous Exponential Model: x(t) = x₀ × eᵏᵗ</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          In continuous physical, chemical, and radiological processes, change occurs instantaneously at every moment rather than in distinct annual or daily steps. This continuous model uses Euler's constant <em>e ≈ 2.71828</em>:
        </p>
        <div class="my-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 font-mono text-center text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-800 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950 dark:text-slate-200">
          x(t) = x₀ × eᵏᵗ
        </div>
        <p>
          The exact algebraic equivalence between the periodic percentage rate <em>r</em> and the continuous rate constant <em>k</em> is:
        </p>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-3 text-xs font-mono dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950 text-center">
          1 + r / 100 = eᵏ  ⟹  k = ln(1 + r / 100)  and  r = 100 × (eᵏ − 1)
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">How Small Growth Rate Differences Compound Dramatically</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
        Because compounding works through powers rather than multiplication by a scalar, even minor percentage rate differences yield enormous disparities over extended periods:
      </p>
