            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Real-World Applications of Exponential Change</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mt-3 text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-3.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white block mb-1">🧫 Bacterial & Cellular Cultures:</strong>
          Under optimal lab conditions with abundant nutrients, bacteria reproduce through binary fission, doubling population count on fixed intervals.
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-3.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white block mb-1">☢️ Radioactive Isotope Decay:</strong>
          Unstable atomic nuclei undergo spontaneous radioactive decay following a constant half-life, critical for carbon dating and nuclear medicine.
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-3.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white block mb-1">💰 Capital & Compound Interest:</strong>
          Investments that earn interest on both initial principal and previously earned interest follow exponential trajectories over decades.
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-3.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white block mb-1">💊 Pharmacokinetics & Elimination:</strong>
          The bodily elimination of most pharmaceutical compounds follows first-order exponential decay kinetics based on a metabolic half-life.
