    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Limitations of Pure Exponential Models</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          While exponential equations provide elegant local approximations, <strong>unconstrained exponential growth cannot continue indefinitely in any finite physical system</strong>. Environmental boundaries eventually intervene:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          <li><strong>Carrying Capacity:</strong> Biological populations eventually face resource limits (food, space, predators), transitioning from exponential growth to an S-shaped <em>logistic curve</em>.</li>
          <li><strong>Market Saturation:</strong> Business customer adoption slows as the addressable market becomes saturated.</li>
          <li><strong>Depletion Effects:</strong> Decaying substances or declining assets approach asymptotic floors or experience altering physical dynamics.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
